 high blood sugar can damage blood vessels and the nerves that control your heart. People with diabetes are more likely to have other conditions that raise the risk for heart disease:\nHigh blood pressure increases the force of blood through your arteries and can damage artery walls. Having both high blood pressure and diabetes can greatly increase your risk for heart disease.\nToo much LDL (\"bad\") cholesterol in your bloodstream can form plaque on damaged artery walls.\nTriglycerides are a type of fat in your blood. High t riglycerides and low HDL (\"good\") cholesterol or high LDL cholesterol contributes to hardening of the arteries.\nThese factors can also raise your risk for heart disease:\nBeing overweight or having obesity\nNot getting enough physical activity\nEating a diet high in saturated fat, trans fat, cholesterol, and salt\nDrinking too much alcohol", `title`: "Bệnh tim mạch và đái tháo đường — nguồn web tự động", `topic`: "Bệnh tim mạch và đái tháo đường", `url`: "https://www.cdc.gov/diabetes/diabetes-complications/diabetes-and-your-heart.html", `web_source_id`: "cdc-heart"};
