The A1C test should not be used to diagnose type 1 diabetes , gestational diabetes , or cystic fibrosis -related diabetes. The A1C test may give false results in people with certain conditions .\nHaving prediabetes is a risk factor for developing type 2 diabetes. Within the prediabetes A1C range of 5.7 to 6.4 percent, the higher the A1C, the greater the risk of diabetes.\nIs the A1C test used during pregnancy?", `title`: "HbA1c: ý nghĩa, giới hạn và chẩn đoán — nguồn web tự động", `topic`: "HbA1c: ý nghĩa, giới hạn và chẩn đoán", `url`: "https://www.niddk.nih.gov/health-information/diagnostic-tests/a1c-test", `web_source_id`: "niddk-a1c"};
