DK Director Dr. Griffin P. Rodgers explaining the importance of participating in clinical trials.\nWhat clinical studies on continuous glucose monitors are looking for participants?\nYou can view a filtered list of clinical studies that use CGMs and are federally funded, open, and recruiting at ClinicalTrials.gov . You can expand or narrow the list to include clinical studies from industry, universities, and individuals; however, the National Institutes of Health does not review these studies and cannot ensure they are safe. Always talk with your health care provider before you participate in a clinical study.\n[1] American Diabetes Association. 7. Diabetes technology: standards of medical care in diabetes—2023. Diabetes Care . 2023;46(Suppl_1):S111–S127. doi.org/10.2337/dc23-S007\n[2] Bantle JP, Thomas W. Glucose measurement in patients with diabetes mellitus with dermal interstitial fluid. Journal of Laboratory and Clinical Medicine . 1997;130(4):436–441. doi:10/10/1016/s0022-2143(97)90044-5", `title`: "Theo dõi glucose liên tục CGM — nguồn web tự động", `topic`: "Theo dõi glucose liên tục CGM", `url`: "https://www.niddk.nih.gov/health-information/diabetes/overview/managing-diabetes/continuous-glucose-monitoring", `web_source_id`: "niddk-cgm"};
