drates to keep blood glucose levels from rising too high after you eat. If you develop low blood glucose while taking these medicines, you will need to take glucose tablets or glucose gel right away. Eating or drinking other sources of carbohydrates won’t raise your blood glucose level quickly enough.\nWhat if I have severe low blood glucose and can’t treat myself?\nGlucagon —a hormone that raises blood glucose levels—is the best way to treat severely low blood glucose. Available as an injection or a nasal spray, glucagon will quickly raise your blood glucose level. Your doctor can prescribe you a glucagon kit for use in case of an emergency.\nIf your blood glucose level drops very low, you won’t be able to treat it by yourself. Be prepared to address severely low blood glucose by\ntalking with your doctor or health care team about when and how to use a glucagon emergency kit. If you have an emergency kit, regularly check the date on the package to make sure it hasn’t expired.", `title`: "Hạ đường huyết: nhận biết và xử trí — nguồn web tự động", `topic`: "Hạ đường huyết: nhận biết và xử trí", `url`: "https://www.niddk.nih.gov/health-information/diabetes/overview/preventing-problems/low-blood-glucose-hypoglycemia", `web_source_id`: "niddk-hypoglycemia"};
