ally if you have diabetes. Both smoking and diabetes can make your blood vessels narrow. E-cigarettes aren’t a safe option either. If you smoke, vape, or use other tobacco products, stop. Ask for help so you don’t have to do it alone.\nHow can a healthy lifestyle help manage my diabetes?\nStaying healthy when you have diabetes can be a challenge. But leading a healthy lifestyle may help keep your blood glucose, blood pressure, and cholesterol levels in the ranges recommended by your health care team.\nCreate a healthy meal plan\nYou may worry that having diabetes means going without foods you enjoy. The good news is that you can still eat your favorite foods, but you might need to eat smaller portions or enjoy them less often. Work with your health care team, which may include a registered dietitian or a diabetes educator , to create a meal plan that works for you.", `title`: "Quản lý bệnh và tầm soát biến chứng — nguồn web tự động", `topic`: "Quản lý bệnh và tầm soát biến chứng", `url`: "https://www.niddk.nih.gov/health-information/diabetes/overview/managing-diabetes", `web_source_id`: "niddk-management"};
