ose level is too low, it is called hypoglycemia . For most people with diabetes, the blood glucose level is too low when it is below 70 mg/dL. 1,2 Talk with your primary care professional or health care team if you often have low blood glucose levels. Some people with low blood glucose experience symptoms such as\nIf you often have low blood glucose levels, you may need to change your diabetes meal plan, physical activity plan, or medicines. Very low blood glucose may lead to confusion or fainting , and it can become a serious medical emergency that must be treated right away.\nGlucagon—a hormone that raises blood glucose levels—is the best way to treat severely low blood glucose . Ask your health care team if you need a prescription for glucagon. If you have a glucagon prescription, you should teach your family, friends, and coworkers when and how to give you glucagon in case you are not able to do it yourself.", `title`: "Quản lý bệnh và tầm soát biến chứng — nguồn web tự động", `topic`: "Quản lý bệnh và tầm soát biến chứng", `url`: "https://www.niddk.nih.gov/health-information/diabetes/overview/managing-diabetes", `web_source_id`: "niddk-management"};
