d_web", `text`: "If you have health problems related to insulin resistance and prediabetes , your health care professional may prescribe other medicines, such as medicines to lower blood pressure or triglyceride levels.\nClinical Trials for Insulin Resistance and Prediabetes\nNIDDK conducts and supports clinical trials in many diseases and conditions, including diabetes. The trials look to find new ways to prevent, detect, or treat disease and improve quality of life.\nWhat are clinical trials for insulin resistance and prediabetes?\nClinical trials—and other types of clinical studies —are part of medical research and involve people like you. When you volunteer to take part in a clinical study, you help doctors and researchers learn more about disease and improve health care for people in the future.\nResearchers are studying many aspects of insulin resistance and prediabetes, such as\nhow diet and exercise affect insulin resistance in older adults\nhow some fats can produce insulin resistance in the muscles\nhow medicines, such as metformin, affect people with prediabetes and heart and blood vessel problems\nFind out if clinical studies are right for you .", `title`: "Tiền tiểu đường và kháng insulin — nguồn web tự động", `topic`: "Tiền tiểu đường và kháng insulin", `url`: "https://www.niddk.nih.gov/health-information/diabetes/overview/what-is-diabetes/prediabetes-insulin-resistance", `web_source_id`: "niddk-prediabetes"};
