finding it hard to get pregnant, talk with your health care professional to find out if you need any further evaluation. Diabetes may produce health problems such as erectile dysfunction and infertility .\nWhat should I do if I have diabetes and I am pregnant?\nIf you have diabetes and you find out that you are pregnant, talk with your health care professional as soon as possible about how to manage your diabetes during your pregnancy. Your target blood glucose level range may be different when you are pregnant than before pregnancy. Working with your health care team and following your plan to manage diabetes can help you have a healthy pregnancy and a healthy baby.", `title`: "Thai kỳ khi đã mắc đái tháo đường — nguồn web tự động", `topic`: "Thai kỳ khi đã mắc đái tháo đường", `url`: "https://www.niddk.nih.gov/health-information/diabetes/diabetes-pregnancy", `web_source_id`: "niddk-pregnancy"};
