d_web", `text`: "If you do not have diabetes but your parent or sibling has type 1 diabetes, your doctor might give you this test to see if you have a higher risk of developing type 1 diabetes. You may want to learn about diabetes symptoms and have follow-up testing as recommended by your doctor. 1\n[1] American Diabetes Association Professional Practice Committee. Standards of medical care in diabetes—2022. Diabetes Care . 2022;45(suppl 1):1–16.7\nThis content is provided as a service of the National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases (NIDDK), part of the National Institutes of Health. NIDDK translates and disseminates research findings to increase knowledge and understanding about health and disease among patients, health professionals, and the public. Content produced by NIDDK is carefully reviewed by NIDDK scientists and other experts.\nThe NIDDK would like to thank: Randy Little, Ph.D., University of Missouri", `title`: "Xét nghiệm và chẩn đoán đái tháo đường — nguồn web tự động", `topic`: "Xét nghiệm và chẩn đoán đái tháo đường", `url`: "https://www.niddk.nih.gov/health-information/diabetes/overview/tests-diagnosis", `web_source_id`: "niddk-tests"};
